    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d578">

                <pb facs="0807" n="793" sameAs="frus:frus1944v06/pg793"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">761.93/1779</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Under Secretary of State</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Stettinius</hi>)<anchor n="50" xml:id="d578-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1944-05-23">May 23, 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>In talking to me yesterday afternoon before preparing to leave to return to his
                    post, Ambassador Harriman said the President requested him to do the
                    following:</p>
                <p>Discuss with Molotov the Chinese situation, particularly Molotov’s, purported
                    complaints against the Chungking government.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>E[<hi rendition="#small-caps">dward</hi>] S[<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >tettinius</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d578-f1" n="50" type="source" xml:id="d578-f1-content">
                <p>Addressed to the Director and the Deputy Director of the Office of Far Eastern
                    Affairs (Grew and Ballantine).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
